  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Saving Children on the Roads in Sierra Leone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">At least 32 children died in 2020 due to road accidents in Sierra Leone. This is a tragedy that happens all too often, with most fatalities occurring while children are either going to school or on their way back home. The Youth Partnership for Peace and Development (YPPD) is working to change this, with programs that educate both children and adults on road safety. YPPD also works with over 200 hundred schools, 400 teachers, and 300 youth, ensuring the constant protection of children.</narrative>
  </description>
